From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:31:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] videoplayer: Hable is the default tone mapping method

An HDR10 video on an SDR display plays through Kodi's tone mapping
shader. Upstream made Hable the method for a saved file without the key
(0bb1747a9a4b) but left the constructor's default at off, and a new
profile's first save writes the constructor's value: every profile ends
up with the method off, and such a video is washed out until the viewer
finds the video settings.

The constructor's default is Hable now, the one method of the three
that is close to a reference (yblod/docs/plans/SDR-OUTPUT-PLAN.md).
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoSettings.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoSettings.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoSettings.cpp
index 0589484..8448497 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoSettings.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoSettings.cpp
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ CVideoSettings::CVideoSettings()
   m_StereoMode = 0;
   m_StereoInvert = false;
   m_VideoStream = -1;
-  m_ToneMapMethod = VS_TONEMAPMETHOD_OFF;
+  m_ToneMapMethod = VS_TONEMAPMETHOD_HABLE;
   m_ToneMapParam = 1.0f;
   m_Orientation = 0;
   m_CenterMixLevel = 0;
